        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Cognitive Dissonance: Performing Menial Tasks</title>\n<script>\nwindow.MathJax = {\n  tex: { inlineMath: [['$', '$']], displayMath: [['$$', '$$']] }\n};\n</script>\n<script id=\"MathJax-script\" async src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\"></script>\n<style>\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  body {\n    margin: 0;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    background: #0f2b52;\n    color: #ffffff;\n  }\n  .poster {\n    display: flex;\n    width: 1056px;\n    min-height: 816px;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    background: linear-gradient(120deg, #123769 0%, #1b4d8f 55%, #1667c8 100%);\n  }\n\n  /* ---------- LEFT PANEL ---------- */\n  .left {\n    width: 408px;\n    background: #12294d;\n    padding: 55px 38px 20px 38px;\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n  }\n  .presents {\n    font-size: 19px;\n    line-height: 1.45;\n    color: #ffffff;\n    margin-bottom: 26px;\n  }\n  h1.title {\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-weight: 400;\n    font-size: 47px;\n    line-height: 1.22;\n    margin: 0 0 30px 0;\n    color: #ffffff;\n  }\n  .authors {\n    font-style: italic;\n    font-size: 18px;\n    line-height: 1.5;\n    color: #4aa8e8;\n    margin-bottom: 40px;\n  }\n  .icon-row {\n    display: flex;\n    gap: 22px;\n    margin: 10px 0 40px 0;\n  }\n  .placeholder {\n    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05);\n    border: 1px dashed rgba(255,255,255,0.35);\n    color: #9dc6ee;\n    font-size: 9px;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    text-align: center;\n    padding: 2px;\n    line-height: 1.2;\n  }\n  .head-icon { width: 96px; height: 105px; }\n  .divider {\n    border: 0;\n    border-top: 1px solid #33567f;\n    margin: auto 0 18px 0;\n  }\n  .references {\n    font-size: 9px;\n    line-height: 1.5;\n    color: #dbe6f2;\n    padding-bottom: 30px;\n  }\n  .references .head { letter-spacing: 0.5px; }\n\n  /* ---------- RIGHT PANEL ---------- */\n  .right {\n    flex: 1;\n    padding: 30px 30px 34px 28px;\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n    grid-auto-rows: min-content;\n    gap: 14px 12px;\n    align-content: start;\n  }\n  .card {\n    background: #16305c;\n    padding: 22px 22px 18px 22px;\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n  }\n  .card.dark { background: #122a52; }\n  .card h2 {\n    font-size: 21px;\n    margin: 0 0 14px 0;\n    color: #ffffff;\n  }\n  .card-body {\n    display: flex;\n    gap: 10px;\n  }\n  .card-text {\n    width: 130px;\n    font-size: 11.5px;\n    line-height: 1.42;\n  }\n  .card-text p { margin: 0 0 12px 0; }\n  .card-text p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }\n  .card-icons {\n    flex: 1;\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: flex-start;\n    gap: 12px;\n  }\n  .ic { width: 76px; height: 76px; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"poster\">\n\n  <!-- LEFT COLUMN -->\n  <div class=\"left\">\n    <div class=\"presents\">\n      The National Centre<br>\n      for Neurology and Brain<br>\n      Mechanics Presents\n    </div>\n\n    <h1 class=\"title\">Cognitive Dissonance: Performing Menial Tasks</h1>\n\n    <div class=\"authors\">\n      Study conducted by Jonas Festinger,<br>\n      Marcus Carlsmith &amp; Gabriel Chessman\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"icon-row\">\n      <div class=\"placeholder head-icon\">[Icon: head silhouette with gear]</div>\n      <div class=\"placeholder head-icon\">[Icon: head silhouette with exclamation mark]</div>\n      <div class=\"placeholder head-icon\">[Icon: head silhouette with question mark]</div>\n    </div>\n\n    <hr class=\"divider\">\n\n    <div class=\"references\">\n      <div class=\"head\">REFERENCES:</div>\n      Walsh, Karen., Kemputo, Odelle., &ldquo;The psychology of self-deception&rdquo;<br>\n      The Anaptic Journal, 2017 &bull; Satuda, Evelyn., Temitope, Anya., &ldquo;Neuroscience of Decision-Making&rdquo; The Science Review, 2018 &bull; Brahms, Hansen., Leigh, Anderson., &ldquo;The Need and Neurology for Happiness&rdquo;, The Arch Journal, 2020\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- RIGHT COLUMN GRID -->\n  <div class=\"right\">\n\n    <div class=\"card\">\n      <h2>Purpose:</h2>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <div class=\"card-text\">\n          <p>Festinger, Carlsmith and Chessman wanted to understand if making people perform a menial task would result in cognitive dissonance as a result of forced compliance behavior.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"card-icons\">\n          <div class=\"placeholder ic\">[Icon: gears]</div>\n          <div class=\"placeholder ic\">[Icon: group of people]</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"card dark\">\n      <h2>Hypothesis:</h2>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <div class=\"card-text\">\n          <p>When asked to do an unenjoyable task, people will not readily admit as much, and tell themselves and others it is actually enjoyable.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"card-icons\">\n          <div class=\"placeholder ic\">[Icon: thumbs up]</div>\n          <div class=\"placeholder ic\">[Icon: balance scales]</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"card\">\n      <h2>Participants:</h2>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <div class=\"card-text\">\n          <p>In a lab setting, 71 male students as participants to perform a series of menial tasks (like turning pegs in a peg board for an hour).</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"card-icons\">\n          <div class=\"placeholder ic\">[Icon: clock]</div>\n          <div class=\"placeholder ic\">[Icon: circuit board with magnifier]</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"card dark\">\n      <h2>Method:</h2>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <div class=\"card-text\">\n          <p>The participants were then paid either $1 or $20 to tell a waiting participant (a test confederate) that the tasks were really engaging and fun. Almost all of the participants agreed to walk into the waiting room and persuade the confederate that the boring experiment would be interesting.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"card-icons\">\n          <div class=\"placeholder ic\">[Icon: speech bubble]</div>\n          <div class=\"placeholder ic\">[Icon: hand giving money]</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"card\">\n      <h2>Results:</h2>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <div class=\"card-text\">\n          <p>When the participants were asked to evaluate the experiment, the participants who were paid only $1 rated the tedious task as more fun and enjoyable than the participants who were paid $20 to lie.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"card-icons\">\n          <div class=\"placeholder ic\">[Icon: upward arrow]</div>\n          <div class=\"placeholder ic\">[Icon: star with plus sign]</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"card dark\">\n      <h2>Conclusion:</h2>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <div class=\"card-text\">\n          <p>Getting paid $1 is not sufficient for lying, so those who were paid $1 experienced dissonance. These participants could only overcome that dissonance by coming to believe that the tasks really were interesting and enjoyable.</p>\n          <p>Being paid $20 provides a reason, therefore there is no dissonance.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"card-icons\">\n          <div class=\"placeholder ic\">[Icon: head silhouette with light source]</div>\n          <div class=\"placeholder ic\">[Icon: head silhouette with gear]</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>"
